cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite the manuscript scaffold when a DOI is
  assigned; until then cite this repository for code and aggregate research records.
title: "Project Asma: reproducible investigation of a primary platinum-refractory HGSOC protein signature"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arifuddin
    given-names: Alkindus
  - family-names: Arif
    given-names: Raz
  - name: Foundation Zero
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-11-04
repository-code: "https://github.com/Foundation-0/project-asma"
url: "https://github.com/Foundation-0/project-asma"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Research scaffold honouring Asma Ansari: reproduce and stress-test the
  Chowdhury et al. (Cell 2023) primary platinum-refractory high-grade serous
  ovarian cancer protein signature with labelled claims (PROVEN, VERIFIED,
  KNOWN, CONJECTURE), pinned software checks on synthetic inputs, and bounded
  public-source audits. Not clinical decision support. Code is MIT; text and
  figures are CC BY 4.0; third-party study files retain their own terms (NOTICE).
keywords:
  - ovarian cancer
  - proteomics
  - reproducibility
  - platinum refractory
  - high-grade serous carcinoma
  - research scaffold
